This is to address the above issue seen where the Level shifter (LS) cells were being placed incorrectly to the power grid and this is as it was having a LEF issue. This was also causing M1 shorts internally with the cell
As shown above ? placement was such that VDD pin of cell being connected to VSS and VSS pin of cell being connected to VDD.Below is a workaround to get this resolved
Hacking the LEFs
I?ve already hacked the LEFs and placed them in this area which should be accessible.
/home/adrajesh/common/Desktop/ECE530-2023-SPRING/hacked_lefs/
also here:
/u/bcruik2/hacked_lefs/

For the runs to pick these up, you can edit the script accordingly ? scripts/innovus-get-timlibslefs.tcl 
set lef_path "/home/adrajesh/common/Desktop/ECE530-2023-SPRING/hacked_lefs/saed32nm_hvt_1p9m.lef /home/adrajesh/common/Desktop/ECE530-2023-SPRING/hacked_lefs/saed32nm_lvt_1p9m.lef /home/adrajesh/common/Desktop/ECE530-2023-SPRING/hacked_lefs/saed32nm_rvt_1p9m.lef /pkgs/synopsys/2020/32_28nm/SAED32_EDK/lib/sram/lef/saed32sram.lef"

What changed?
For the LS cells, we introduce a new SITE
Add the ?unitdouble? SITE to the tech lef

You can have copy over the tech lef from this location to your run dir?

cp /home/adrajesh/common/Desktop/ECE530-2023-SPRING/hacked_lefs/tech.lef <work_dir>/cadence_cap_tech/tech.lef

What changed?

We add a ?unitdouble? SITE in the tech lef
After these changes, after init_design is done, you should see your site rows created something like this?

See Word Doc for pictures.

Now if you proceed with your remaining steps and do place_design, your LS cells would snap to the new site row which we defined and would draw power correctly and there won?t be any internal shorts in M1 layer. ?

We would ultimately want our rows to be defined like in the below snap.
